{"q":"236","t":"Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Tree","d":"Medium","p":false,"c":"<p>Given a binary tree, find the lowest common ancestor (LCA) of two given nodes in the tree.</p>\n\n<p>According to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lowest_common_ancestor\" target=\"_blank\">definition of LCA on Wikipedia</a>: &ldquo;The lowest common ancestor is defined between two nodes <code>p</code> and <code>q</code> as the lowest node in <code>T</code> that has both <code>p</code> and <code>q</code> as descendants (where we allow <b>a node to be a descendant of itself</b>).&rdquo;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/e771e2536545b377.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 190px;\" />\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> root = [3,5,1,6,2,0,8,null,null,7,4], p = 5, q = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The LCA of nodes 5 and 1 is 3.\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/e771e2536545b377.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 190px;\" />\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> root = [3,5,1,6,2,0,8,null,null,7,4], p = 5, q = 4\n<strong>Output:</strong> 5\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The LCA of nodes 5 and 4 is 5, since a node can be a descendant of itself according to the LCA definition.\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> root = [1,2], p = 1, q = 2\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range <code>[2, 10<sup>5</sup>]</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>-10<sup>9</sup> &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 10<sup>9</sup></code></li>\n\t<li>All <code>Node.val</code> are <strong>unique</strong>.</li>\n\t<li><code>p != q</code></li>\n\t<li><code>p</code> and <code>q</code> will exist in the tree.</li>\n</ul>\n","h":[],"m":"{\n  \"name\": \"lowestCommonAncestor\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"root\",\n      \"type\": \"TreeNode\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"p\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"q\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"return\": {\n    \"type\": \"TreeNode\"\n  },\n  \"manual\": true\n}","g":[{"name":"Tree","slug":"tree"},{"name":"Depth-First Search","slug":"depth-first-search"},{"name":"Binary Tree","slug":"binary-tree"},{"name":"Binary Lifting","slug":"binary-lifting"},{"name":"Lowest Common Ancestor","slug":"lowest-common-ancestor"}],"s":[{"t":"Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Search Tree","s":"lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-search-tree","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Smallest Common Region","s":"smallest-common-region","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Find Players With Zero or One Losses","s":"find-players-with-zero-or-one-losses","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Tree II","s":"lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-tree-ii","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Tree III","s":"lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-tree-iii","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Tree IV","s":"lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-tree-iv","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Step-By-Step Directions From a Binary Tree Node to Another","s":"step-by-step-directions-from-a-binary-tree-node-to-another","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Cycle Length Queries in a Tree","s":"cycle-length-queries-in-a-tree","d":"Hard","p":false}],"co":[["Amazon","amazon"],["Meta","facebook"],["Google","google"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["BlackRock","blackrock"],["LinkedIn","linkedin"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["Atlassian","atlassian"],["Apple","apple"],["Oracle","oracle"],["Cisco","cisco"],["SAP","sap"],["TikTok","tiktok"],["Yandex","yandex"],["Adobe","adobe"],["Intuit","intuit"],["Intel","intel"],["Wix","wix"]],"cs":{"a":[["Amazon","amazon",13],["Google","google",4],["BlackRock","blackrock",3]],"b":[["Meta","facebook",9],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",5]],"m":[["Microsoft","microsoft",28],["Atlassian","atlassian",18],["LinkedIn","linkedin",13],["Yandex","yandex",9],["Apple","apple",8],["Oracle","oracle",8],["TikTok","tiktok",7],["Adobe","adobe",5],["NewsBreak","newsbreak",5],["Cisco","cisco",2]]}}